issue.body:
**Need:** machine-readable results for every number the paper reports, ideally as `report/results/numbers.tex` (`\newcommand` macros) generated by the code, plus the JSON/CSV it is made from:
- mean accuracy and 95% interval for multinomial LR and for kNN (10×stratified 5-fold, 50 outer folds), with the interval method named (and, if you use it, a corrected-resampled-t (Nadeau–Bengio) interval alongside or instead of the naive t);
- paired difference (LR − kNN) mean and 95% interval, same method;
- the k grid, the inner CV scheme, and the distribution of selected k across outer folds;
- dataset provenance: OpenML id 61, version, n=150, md5/checksum of the downloaded file;
- Ibex job id, node name, local host, software versions, and whether the local and Ibex per-fold results are bitwise identical (and the max abs diff if not);
- LR settings (solver, C, scaling) and kNN settings (scaling, metric).

**For:** the abstract, results paragraph and reproducibility paragraph of `report/report.pdf`; every number there must trace to a file you deliver.

**Waits on it:** the results section of the draft; I write the rest now.
